# Optional overrides for the LOCAL kind stack (scripts/setup.sh).
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# You do NOT need this file to run the demo — every value below has a working
# default and NO credentials are required. Copy it only when you want to change
# something. `.env` is gitignored.
#
# This file configures the self-hosted local stack only. The internal cloud
# deployment (Atlas + Ditto Cloud + Kanopy) is configured through
# environment/*.yaml and Kubernetes Secrets — see
# docs/INTERNAL_DEPLOY_MAINTENANCE.md.

# ── cluster ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# KIND_CLUSTER=tak-situational-demo

# ── Ditto Big Peer ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The hostname ATAK devices use to reach the Big Peer. Leave unset and
# setup.sh derives it from this machine's LAN IP via nip.io, e.g.
#   ditto.192.168.1.23.nip.io
# Set it explicitly if auto-detection picks the wrong interface (VPN, Docker
# bridge, multiple NICs) or if you have real DNS for the host.
# IMPORTANT: it must resolve to THIS machine from the phone's network —
# "localhost" will not work, the phone would resolve it to itself.
# BIG_PEER_HOST=ditto.192.168.1.23.nip.io

# Big Peer release. The Ditto Operator supports >= 1.49.0; >= 1.63.2 includes
# the connector crash-recovery fix. Change this if the pinned tag is not
# available to your Ditto account (setup.sh fails fast on image pull errors).
# BIG_PEER_VERSION=1.63.2

# Ditto Operator chart version (oci://quay.io/ditto-external/ditto-operator).
# The operator is in Private Preview, so CRD fields can move between releases.
# DITTO_OPERATOR_VERSION=0.18.1

# Must match infra/k8s/ditto/20-bigpeerapp.yaml if you change it.
# DITTO_APP_ID=7a9f1c4e-2b6d-4f83-9c15-8e0d3a5b7f42

# ── MongoDB ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DATABASE_NAME=tak_demo
# MCK_VERSION=1.8.1

# ── AI panel (Ollama) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The model must support tool calling — the agent answers only from live
# MongoDB data via four tools. Smaller alternatives: llama3.1:8b, qwen2.5:3b
# (weaker tool use). Keep this in step with LLM_MODEL in infra/local/backend.yaml.
# OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen2.5:7b

# Skip Ollama entirely (saves ~8 GB RAM and a multi-GB model pull). The AI
# panel hides itself when no LLM backend is reachable; everything else works.
# OLLAMA_SKIP=1

# ── pinned component versions (rarely changed) ─────────────────────────────
# WEBAPP_CHART_VERSION=4.30.0
# INGRESS_NGINX_REF=controller-v1.11.3
# CERT_MANAGER_VERSION=v1.16.2
# Strimzi 0.49.0 is the newest release the Ditto Operator supports — 1.x breaks
# the Big Peer controller. Do not bump without checking Ditto's release notes.
# STRIMZI_VERSION=0.49.0
